//@version=6
// ==============================================================================================
//                        F I B O N A C C I   L E V E L   T R A D E S
// ==============================================================================================
//
//  Indicator Name : Fibonacci Level Trades
//  Author         : Michael_Fx_Trader
//  Version        : v6.0 - July 2026
//  Pine Version   : Pine Script v6
//  Script Type    : Overlay indicator (plots on the price chart)
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A U T H O R   V E R I F I C A T I O N   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I am Michael_Fx_Trader, the publisher and sole original author of this exact implementation of
//  "Fibonacci Level Trades." I designed the architecture of this tool, wrote every line of the
//  Pine Script v6 code contained in this file, tested it across multiple asset classes and
//  timeframes, and I take full and sole ownership and responsibility for it.
//
//  Specifically, I independently designed and coded: the volatility-adaptive swing detection that
//  anchors the Fibonacci scale; the automatic direction logic that decides whether the current
//  leg is bullish or bearish and orients the retracement accordingly; the full retracement and
//  extension level engine with its configurable ratios; the Golden Pocket band; the confluence
//  scoring model that combines the reaction at a level with trend agreement, a momentum filter and
//  candle rejection before releasing a signal; the entry, stop and target projection built from
//  the Fibonacci geometry itself; the signal state machine that prevents repeated firing inside one
//  reaction; the alert framework; and the complete dashboard and presentation layer.
//
//  This declaration is made for this specific version of the script (v6.0, July 2026). Any future
//  modified version I publish will carry its own updated declaration in this same header.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  O R I G I N A L   I N D I C A T O R   S C R I P T   I M P L E M E N T A T I O N
//  V E R I F I C A T I O N   A N D   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I verify and declare that this script is an original implementation authored from scratch by
//  Michael_Fx_Trader. No portion of this code was copied, ported, decompiled, translated,
//  reverse-engineered or adapted from any other author's closed-source, invite-only, protected or
//  open-source script. No third-party library and no republished open-source script forms any part
//  of this work, and no other author's signal logic or visual system was reproduced.
//
//  I acknowledge openly that the underlying mathematics is public and belongs to no author. The
//  Fibonacci sequence and the ratios derived from it, including 0.236, 0.382, 0.5, 0.618, 0.786
//  and the extensions beyond 1.0, are centuries-old public mathematics. Their use in charting as
//  retracement and extension levels, the notion of a Golden Pocket around 0.618 to 0.65, and the
//  practice of anchoring the scale between a swing high and a swing low, are all common knowledge
//  taught freely across the trading community and owned by no one.
//
//  My original contribution, and what this declaration covers, is the specific code
//  implementation: my own adaptive swing anchoring, my own direction and orientation logic, my own
//  confluence scoring model, my own signal state machine, my own Fibonacci-derived trade
//  projection, and my own presentation layer. Conceptual overlap with other Fibonacci tools is
//  therefore unavoidable and expected, since we are all drawing the same public ratios, but there
//  is no source-code overlap of any kind with any other author's work.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  W H A T   T H I S   I N D I C A T O R   D O E S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Fibonacci Level Trades draws the Fibonacci retracement and extension of the current swing
//  automatically, watches how price reacts at those levels, and only when a reaction is confirmed
//  by trend, momentum and candle rejection does it mark a buy or a sell.
//
//  1) ADAPTIVE SWING ANCHORING
//     The scale is anchored between the most recent significant swing high and swing low. The
//     confirmation window for those swings widens and narrows with volatility, so the anchor stays
//     meaningful whether the market is fast or slow, and the levels re-draw as new swings form.
//
//  2) DIRECTION AND ORIENTATION
//     The engine decides whether the active leg is bullish or bearish and orients the retracement
//     correctly: measured from swing low to swing high in an up-leg, and from swing high to swing
//     low in a down-leg. The zero and one-hundred percent ends are placed accordingly.
//
//  3) RETRACEMENT AND EXTENSION LEVELS
//     Every standard ratio is drawn and labelled with its price: 0.236, 0.382, 0.5, 0.618, 0.786,
//     the 1.0 origin, and the extensions 1.272, 1.618 and 2.618 for targets. Each ratio can be
//     switched off individually.
//
//  4) THE GOLDEN POCKET
//     The band between 0.618 and 0.65 is shaded separately, because it is the area traders watch
//     most closely for a reaction.
//
//  5) CONFLUENCE-SCORED SIGNALS
//     A level touch alone is never enough. When price reaches a chosen entry zone, the engine
//     scores the setup on four things: the reaction at the level, agreement with the higher-level
//     trend, a momentum filter, and a candle rejection at the level. Only when the score clears the
//     threshold is a buy or sell released, so signals fire on genuine reactions rather than on
//     every touch.
//
//  6) TRADE PROJECTION
//     On a signal, entry, stop and targets are projected from the Fibonacci geometry itself: the
//     stop beyond the next retracement level, the targets at the swing origin and the extensions.
//     Levels are drawn as clean lines and can carry optional labels.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  U N I V E R S A L   M A R K E T   A N D   T I M E F R A M E   C O M P A T I B I L I T Y
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  The Fibonacci ratios are pure proportions, so nothing in this tool depends on price magnitude.
//  The swing window, the momentum filter and every distance are expressed in ATR or as ratios, so
//  no pip value, point distance or price constant appears anywhere. The same settings behave
//  correctly on Forex, gold and other metals, indices, crypto, futures and equities, from seconds
//  charts to monthly. No volume data is required.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  L I V E   B E H A V I O U R   A N D   R E P A I N T I N G   S T A T E M E N T
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A swing is confirmed only after the required bars have formed to its right, which is inherent
//  to every swing-based tool. Once confirmed, that swing anchor is fixed and the levels drawn from
//  it do not move until a new swing replaces the anchor, at which point the scale re-draws to the
//  new leg. This is the normal and expected behaviour of an automatic Fibonacci tool.
//
//  Signals are confirmed on bar close and do not repaint: a printed buy or sell never disappears
//  from history. No request.security call is used, so there is no higher-timeframe lookahead of any
//  kind.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  H O N E S T   N O T E
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Fibonacci levels do not predict price. They mark proportional areas where many traders place
//  orders, which is part of why price reacts there at all. This tool adds trend, momentum and
//  rejection filters so that it signals on confirmed reactions rather than on hope, but no level
//  holds every time, and the confluence score is a filter, not a probability or a guarantee. Use
//  the stop on every trade.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D I S C L A I M E R
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  This tool is for educational and informational purposes only. It does not constitute financial
//  advice. Trading involves risk; past patterns do not guarantee future results. Use proper risk
//  management and consult a licensed financial advisor before trading real capital.
// ==============================================================================================

indicator("Fibonacci Level Trades", "Fib Trades", overlay = true, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 100)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I N P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
gSw = "=====  SWING ANCHOR  ====="
minSwing = input.int(5,  "Minimum Swing Bars", minval = 2, maxval = 30, group = gSw, tooltip = "Confirmation bars on each side of a swing when volatility is high.")
maxSwing = input.int(15, "Maximum Swing Bars", minval = 3, maxval = 60, group = gSw, tooltip = "Confirmation bars when volatility is low.")
atrLen   = input.int(14, "ATR Length", minval = 2, maxval = 200, group = gSw)
volFast  = input.int(10, "Volatility Fast ATR", minval = 2, maxval = 100, group = gSw)
volSlow  = input.int(50, "Volatility Slow ATR", minval = 5, maxval = 300, group = gSw)

gFib = "=====  FIBONACCI LEVELS  ====="
show236 = input.bool(true,  "0.236", group = gFib, inline = "r1")
show382 = input.bool(true,  "0.382", group = gFib, inline = "r1")
show500 = input.bool(true,  "0.5",   group = gFib, inline = "r1")
show618 = input.bool(true,  "0.618", group = gFib, inline = "r2")
show786 = input.bool(true,  "0.786", group = gFib, inline = "r2")
show1000= input.bool(true,  "1.0",   group = gFib, inline = "r2")
showExt = input.bool(true,  "Extensions (1.272 / 1.618 / 2.618)", group = gFib)
goldPkt = input.bool(true,  "Shade Golden Pocket (0.618-0.65)", group = gFib)
lvlExtend= input.int(40, "Level Extend (bars)", minval = 0, maxval = 300, group = gFib)
showLvlLbl= input.bool(true, "Show Level Prices", group = gFib)

gSig = "=====  SIGNAL ENGINE  ====="
entryLo  = input.float(0.618, "Entry Zone Start", minval = 0.1, maxval = 0.9, step = 0.001, group = gSig, tooltip = "Signals are hunted while price is inside this retracement band.")
entryHi  = input.float(0.786, "Entry Zone End",   minval = 0.1, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.001, group = gSig)
minScore = input.float(3.0, "Minimum Confluence Score (0-4)", minval = 1, maxval = 4, step = 0.5, group = gSig, tooltip = "How many of the four confluence factors must agree before a signal fires.")
useTrend = input.bool(true, "Require Trend Agreement", group = gSig)
trendLen = input.int(50, "Trend EMA Length", minval = 5, maxval = 400, group = gSig)
useMom   = input.bool(true, "Require Momentum Filter", group = gSig)
rsiLen   = input.int(14, "RSI Length", minval = 2, maxval = 100, group = gSig)
useRej   = input.bool(true, "Require Candle Rejection", group = gSig)
cooldown = input.int(6, "Bars Between Signals", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = gSig)

gTr = "=====  TRADE PROJECTION  ====="
showTrade = input.bool(true, "Show Entry / Stop / Target Lines", group = gTr)
stopBeyond= input.float(0.10, "Stop Beyond Anchor (x leg)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 0.5, step = 0.01, group = gTr, tooltip = "How far beyond the 1.0 anchor the stop sits, as a fraction of the swing leg.")
tp1Ext    = input.float(0.0,   "Target 1 (0 = swing origin)", minval = 0, maxval = 3, step = 0.001, group = gTr)
tp2Ext    = input.float(1.272, "Target 2 (extension)", minval = 1, maxval = 5, step = 0.001, group = gTr)
tp3Ext    = input.float(1.618, "Target 3 (extension)", minval = 1, maxval = 5, step = 0.001, group = gTr)
showTradeLbl = input.bool(false, "Show Trade Level Labels", group = gTr, tooltip = "OFF draws clean lines only. ON prints ENTRY, STOP and TARGET text.")
tradeExt  = input.int(30, "Trade Line Extend (bars)", minval = 5, maxval = 200, group = gTr)

gDash = "=====  DASHBOARD  ====="
showDash = input.bool(true, "Show Dashboard", group = gDash)
dashPos  = input.string("Top Right", "Position", options = ["Top Right", "Middle Right", "Bottom Right", "Top Left", "Bottom Left"], group = gDash)

gSty = "=====  STYLE  ====="
colBull = input.color(#26a69a, "Bullish", group = gSty, inline = "a")
colBear = input.color(#ef5350, "Bearish", group = gSty, inline = "a")
colFib  = input.color(#8e9aaf, "Fib Lines", group = gSty)
colGold = input.color(#f0b90b, "Golden Pocket", group = gSty)
colDashB= input.color(#0b1020, "Dashboard Background", group = gSty)
colDashT= input.color(#d1d4dc, "Dashboard Text", group = gSty)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A D A P T I V E   S W I N G   W I N D O W
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float atr     = ta.atr(atrLen)
float aFast   = ta.atr(volFast)
float aSlow   = ta.atr(volSlow)
float volRat  = aSlow > 0 ? aFast / aSlow : 1.0
float volRank = nz(ta.percentrank(volRat, 100), 50.0)
int   hiSw    = math.max(minSwing, maxSwing)
int   swLen   = math.max(minSwing, math.min(hiSw, int(math.round(hiSw - (hiSw - minSwing) * volRank / 100.0))))

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  S W I N G   D E T E C T I O N   A N D   A N C H O R
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float ph = ta.pivothigh(high, swLen, swLen)
float pl = ta.pivotlow(low,  swLen, swLen)

var float swHi   = na
var int   swHiBar= na
var float swLo   = na
var int   swLoBar= na

if not na(ph)
    swHi := ph
    swHiBar := bar_index - swLen
if not na(pl)
    swLo := pl
    swLoBar := bar_index - swLen

// the active leg: whichever swing is more recent defines direction
// up-leg  = last confirmed low is older than last high -> measured low(0.0) to high(1.0 side)... we orient below
bool haveBoth = not na(swHi) and not na(swLo)
bool upLeg = haveBoth and nz(swLoBar) < nz(swHiBar)   // low came first, then high -> bullish leg

float anchorHi = swHi
float anchorLo = swLo
float leg = na
if haveBoth
    leg := anchorHi - anchorLo

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  F I B O N A C C I   L E V E L   G E O M E T R Y
//  In an up-leg, 0.0 sits at the swing high and 1.0 at the swing low, so a retracement fraction f
//  gives price = high - leg * f (price pulling back down from the high). In a down-leg it mirrors.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
fibPrice(float f) =>
    na(leg) ? na : upLeg ? anchorHi - leg * f : anchorLo + leg * f

// current retracement fraction of price within the leg (0 at the extreme price ran to, 1 at origin)
float retrac = na
if haveBoth and leg != 0
    retrac := upLeg ? (anchorHi - close) / leg : (close - anchorLo) / leg
retrac := na(retrac) ? na : math.max(-1.0, math.min(3.0, retrac))

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  C O N F L U E N C E   I N P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float emaTrend = ta.ema(close, trendLen)
bool  trendUp  = close > emaTrend and emaTrend > emaTrend[1]
bool  trendDn  = close < emaTrend and emaTrend < emaTrend[1]

float rsi = ta.rsi(close, rsiLen)
bool  momUp = rsi > 45 and rsi > rsi[1]
bool  momDn = rsi < 55 and rsi < rsi[1]

// candle rejection: lower wick for longs, upper wick for shorts
float rng  = high - low
float body = math.abs(close - open)
float lowWick = math.min(open, close) - low
float upWick  = high - math.max(open, close)
bool  bullRej = rng > 0 and lowWick > body * 0.8 and close > open
bool  bearRej = rng > 0 and upWick  > body * 0.8 and close < open

// price inside the entry retracement band
bool inZone = not na(retrac) and retrac >= math.min(entryLo, entryHi) and retrac <= math.max(entryLo, entryHi)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  S I G N A L   S C O R I N G   A N D   S T A T E   M A C H I N E
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// A long is only valid on an up-leg pullback; a short only on a down-leg pullback.
float longScore = 0.0
float shortScore = 0.0

if inZone
    // reaction: price turning back up (long) / down (short) off the zone
    bool reactUp = close > close[1] and low <= fibPrice(math.max(entryLo, entryHi))
    bool reactDn = close < close[1] and high >= fibPrice(math.max(entryLo, entryHi))

    longScore += reactUp ? 1.0 : 0.0
    longScore += (not useTrend or trendUp) ? 1.0 : 0.0
    longScore += (not useMom or momUp) ? 1.0 : 0.0
    longScore += (not useRej or bullRej) ? 1.0 : 0.0

    shortScore += reactDn ? 1.0 : 0.0
    shortScore += (not useTrend or trendDn) ? 1.0 : 0.0
    shortScore += (not useMom or momDn) ? 1.0 : 0.0
    shortScore += (not useRej or bearRej) ? 1.0 : 0.0

var int lastSig = -100000
bool gap = (bar_index - lastSig) > cooldown

bool longRaw  = upLeg     and inZone and longScore  >= minScore and gap
bool shortRaw = not upLeg and inZone and shortScore >= minScore and gap

bool longSig  = longRaw  and barstate.isconfirmed
bool shortSig = shortRaw and barstate.isconfirmed

var int   posDir  = 0
var float entryPx = na
var float stopPx  = na
var float t1Px = na
var float t2Px = na
var float t3Px = na

if longSig or shortSig
    lastSig := bar_index
    posDir  := longSig ? 1 : -1
    entryPx := close
    if longSig
        stopPx := anchorLo - math.abs(leg) * stopBeyond
        t1Px := tp1Ext == 0 ? anchorHi : fibPrice(-(tp1Ext - 1))
        t2Px := anchorLo + math.abs(leg) * tp2Ext
        t3Px := anchorLo + math.abs(leg) * tp3Ext
    else
        stopPx := anchorHi + math.abs(leg) * stopBeyond
        t1Px := tp1Ext == 0 ? anchorLo : fibPrice(-(tp1Ext - 1))
        t2Px := anchorHi - math.abs(leg) * tp2Ext
        t3Px := anchorHi - math.abs(leg) * tp3Ext

float rr = not na(entryPx) and not na(stopPx) and not na(t2Px) and math.abs(entryPx - stopPx) > 0 ? math.abs(t2Px - entryPx) / math.abs(entryPx - stopPx) : na

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D R A W I N G   -   F I B O N A C C I   L E V E L S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
type FibLine
    line ln
    label lb

var array<FibLine> fibDraw = array.new<FibLine>()
var box goldBox = na

drawFib(bool on, float f, string name, color c, int w) =>
    if on and haveBoth and not na(leg) and leg != 0
        float p = fibPrice(f)
        if not na(p)
            int lx = math.min(nz(swHiBar, bar_index), nz(swLoBar, bar_index))
            FibLine fl = FibLine.new()
            fl.ln := line.new(lx, p, bar_index + lvlExtend, p, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(c, 30), width = w)
            if showLvlLbl
                fl.lb := label.new(bar_index + lvlExtend, p, str.tostring(f, "0.###") + "  " + str.tostring(p, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(c, 80), textcolor = color.new(c, 0), size = size.tiny)
            fibDraw.push(fl)

if barstate.islast
    if fibDraw.size() > 0
        for fl in fibDraw
            line.delete(fl.ln)
            label.delete(fl.lb)
        fibDraw.clear()
    box.delete(goldBox)

    if haveBoth and not na(leg) and leg != 0
        color legC = upLeg ? colBull : colBear
        drawFib(true,     0.0,   "0.0",   legC, 2)
        drawFib(show236,  0.236, "0.236", colFib, 1)
        drawFib(show382,  0.382, "0.382", colFib, 1)
        drawFib(show500,  0.5,   "0.5",   colFib, 1)
        drawFib(show618,  0.618, "0.618", colGold, 1)
        drawFib(show786,  0.786, "0.786", colFib, 1)
        drawFib(show1000, 1.0,   "1.0",   legC, 2)
        if showExt
            drawFib(true, 1.272, "1.272", colFib, 1)
            drawFib(true, 1.618, "1.618", colFib, 1)
            drawFib(true, 2.618, "2.618", colFib, 1)

        if goldPkt
            float g1 = fibPrice(0.618)
            float g2 = fibPrice(0.65)
            int lx = math.min(nz(swHiBar, bar_index), nz(swLoBar, bar_index))
            goldBox := box.new(lx, math.max(g1, g2), bar_index + lvlExtend, math.min(g1, g2), xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = color.new(colGold, 60), bgcolor = color.new(colGold, 82))

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D R A W I N G   -   S I G N A L S   A N D   T R A D E   L E V E L S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
plotshape(longSig,  "Buy",  shape.labelup,   location.belowbar, color = colBull, textcolor = color.white, text = "BUY",  size = size.small)
plotshape(shortSig, "Sell", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color = colBear, textcolor = color.white, text = "SELL", size = size.small)

var line  enL = na
var line  slL = na
var line  t1L = na
var line  t2L = na
var line  t3L = na
var label enLb = na
var label slLb = na
var label t1Lb = na
var label t2Lb = na
var label t3Lb = na

if showTrade and (longSig or shortSig)
    line.delete(enL)
    line.delete(slL)
    line.delete(t1L)
    line.delete(t2L)
    line.delete(t3L)
    label.delete(enLb)
    label.delete(slLb)
    label.delete(t1Lb)
    label.delete(t2Lb)
    label.delete(t3Lb)

    color dir = posDir == 1 ? colBull : colBear
    int rx = bar_index + tradeExt

    enL := line.new(bar_index, entryPx, rx, entryPx, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(dir, 10), width = 2)
    slL := line.new(bar_index, stopPx,  rx, stopPx,  xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colBear, 20), style = line.style_dashed)
    t1L := line.new(bar_index, t1Px, rx, t1Px, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colBull, 30), style = line.style_dotted)
    t2L := line.new(bar_index, t2Px, rx, t2Px, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colBull, 25), style = line.style_dotted)
    t3L := line.new(bar_index, t3Px, rx, t3Px, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colBull, 20), style = line.style_dotted)

    if showTradeLbl
        enLb := label.new(rx, entryPx, "ENTRY " + str.tostring(entryPx, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(dir, 20), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
        slLb := label.new(rx, stopPx,  "STOP "  + str.tostring(stopPx,  format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(colBear, 20), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
        t1Lb := label.new(rx, t1Px, "TP1 " + str.tostring(t1Px, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(colBull, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
        t2Lb := label.new(rx, t2Px, "TP2 " + str.tostring(t2Px, format.mintick) + (na(rr) ? "" : "   " + str.tostring(rr, "#.#") + "R"), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(colBull, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
        t3Lb := label.new(rx, t3Px, "TP3 " + str.tostring(t3Px, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(colBull, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D A S H B O A R D
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var table dash = na

dashPosition() =>
    dashPos == "Middle Right" ? position.middle_right : dashPos == "Bottom Right" ? position.bottom_right : dashPos == "Top Left" ? position.top_left : dashPos == "Bottom Left" ? position.bottom_left : position.top_right

if barstate.islast and showDash
    table.delete(dash)
    dash := table.new(dashPosition(), 2, 8, border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(colDashT, 85), frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.new(colDashT, 75))

    color bgH = color.new(colDashB, 0)
    color bgR = color.new(colDashB, 14)
    color dim = color.new(colDashT, 45)

    string legTxt = not haveBoth ? "building" : upLeg ? "BULLISH LEG" : "BEARISH LEG"
    color  legCol = not haveBoth ? dim : upLeg ? colBull : colBear
    string posTxt = posDir == 1 ? "LONG ACTIVE" : posDir == -1 ? "SHORT ACTIVE" : "flat"
    color  posCol = posDir == 1 ? colBull : posDir == -1 ? colBear : dim

    table.cell(dash, 0, 0, "FIBONACCI LEVEL TRADES", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = colGold, text_size = size.small)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 0, 1, 0)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 1, "Active Leg", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 1, legTxt, bgcolor = bgR, text_color = legCol, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 2, "Retracement", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 2, na(retrac) ? "-" : str.tostring(retrac * 100, "#.#") + "%", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = not na(retrac) and retrac >= 0.618 and retrac <= 0.65 ? colGold : colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 3, "In Entry Zone", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 3, inZone ? "YES" : "no", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = inZone ? colGold : dim, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 4, "Confluence", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 4, str.tostring(math.max(longScore, shortScore), "#.0") + " / 4   (need " + str.tostring(minScore, "#.#") + ")", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = math.max(longScore, shortScore) >= minScore ? colBull : dim, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 5, "Trend / Momentum", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 5, (trendUp ? "Up" : trendDn ? "Down" : "Flat") + "  /  RSI " + str.tostring(rsi, "#"), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = trendUp ? colBull : trendDn ? colBear : dim, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 6, "Position", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 6, posTxt, bgcolor = bgR, text_color = posCol, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 7, "Last Trade R:R", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 7, na(rr) ? "-" : str.tostring(rr, "#.##") + "R", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A L E R T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
alertcondition(longSig,  "Fib - Buy Signal",  "Fibonacci Level Trades: buy signal at a Fibonacci level on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(shortSig, "Fib - Sell Signal", "Fibonacci Level Trades: sell signal at a Fibonacci level on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(inZone and not inZone[1], "Fib - Price Entered Golden Zone", "Fibonacci Level Trades: price entered the Fibonacci entry zone on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition((upLeg and not upLeg[1]) or (not upLeg and upLeg[1]), "Fib - Leg Flipped", "Fibonacci Level Trades: the active Fibonacci leg changed direction on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")

if longSig
    alert("Fib Buy - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if shortSig
    alert("Fib Sell - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D A T A   W I N D O W   O U T P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
plot(retrac,   "Retracement Fraction", color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(upLeg ? 1 : 0, "Leg Direction",   color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(math.max(longScore, shortScore), "Confluence Score", color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(posDir,   "Position",             color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
